* A floor read carries no as-of stamp: `standAs` returns a bare class (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/waking-floor">>).
* The boot's order holds four named reds nobody wrote, and they gate any split of the boot by region (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/vessel-regions">>).
* The Handle surface adapters: four surfaces stand as type and vocabulary; loopback first, then DNS control (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/handle-card">>). `lares handle graft` stands as a stub over a built mint, where `publish`, `rotate`, `burn` and `attest` run live; the antigen's ban-`nym` move stays untouched; the browser's publish surface and a phone summons that presents the veil card stay owed. Flagged, unbuilt: a Handle's presenting cabal may also serve as its recovery cabal.
* The hostful code half: `carrierBaseRelPath` discards a hostful URI (`bag-paths.ts`), so a hostful title never sites; one carrier claims otherwise (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/lar-uri-namespace">>).
* Title-to-path persistence: the title-to-base map lives in memory alone (`disk-projector.ts`).
* Wikis-first writes: `meme promote` holds no in-wiki path, and the hand-edit weld stays unbuilt, landing last (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/wiki-layer-ontology">>).
* Live equivocation's prerequisites: `detectDuplicity` runs in tests alone; no watcher plane, no feed adapter, no durable telemetry (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/live-equivocation">>).
* The crossing record's production membrane around the agent worldline (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/api/mandate-activity-provenance">>); its two forks read in #/open.
* Whether the browser shore serves its worn face plane, decided against the typed verified-peer seam that stands (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/research/browser-persona-ring-parity">>).
* Fleet gathering must batch: the one-road delegation cost grows faster than its batch. The petname switcher, the cabal quorum surface for an outward crossing, the browser tier door and the compartment-collector check stand behind it; no live path gathers a fleet yet.
* The self-slot inner ring: it narrows alone, and wiring it freezes a naming (#/open).
* No SES or Compartment realm gate stands in the tree; it gates any live authoring of unpinned code.
* Operator power reaches no browser vessel: a seam enforced by disk access, never a capability. Co-hosted sovereignty between same-uid peers stands claimed and unenforced.
* The crossing rail's three requirements (both ends as presented capabilities, a saga shape, declared deletion semantics) and a realm tally's move onto the shared substrate both stand researched and unbuilt.
* A deny-only antigen share wants entries that can lapse, carried provenance and a merge rule before two lists ever merge.
* Observer-local hardening by silence must BOUND its wait, or a withheld update freezes a victim (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/field-collision">>).
* One charter per vessel rests on a single seal home (`larSealHome`), a guard on one file and never a law; a vessel that carries a second Nexus wants a second seal home, and the charter train names none.
* Realm standing does not cross operators: a feed slot lands in its writer's own daemon bag. The cure points the realm verbs' store at the realm's shared substrate and requires the seal on a foreign slot; the seal verifier holds no caller yet (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/cabal-realm-clock.ts`).
* The bag plane still carries its creator's identifier in the clear on every carried event, where the WHO plane's veil-born group hides it; a fresh measure should confirm it.
* The bag-tier reader takes the hearth's manifest alone; a repository-homed manifest reads VEIL, tighter and never looser.
* A startup module inside the VM, wiring whatever the projection environment lacks, stands held; the off-main-thread engine research may answer it.
* Builds held on purpose, each on the operator's word: the lease cure, the docker partition scenario, WebTransport, the `<<~?` sigil, the SOURCE tiddler.
* Smaller threads: the tombstone and whiteout verb, reserved; Automerge history growth; `lares wiki` subcommands that print for humans alone; an engine-swap reconcile that answered `current` against a stale engine; the NFC assertion at the ingest shore; the parser's retired typed-edge emission plane (`kumu-device.ts`); a `TimeoutNegativeWarning` in e2e runs, unlocalized; the house's register names ahi kā Hawaiian where its documented home reads Māori, and a primary source should settle it.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-trains>>

!! The trains ~ each train's commits in order, what it waits on, and its riskiest step

''Rules every train keeps'': one spirit per commit; every commit leaves HEAD building with its unit
suites green; red first, with a control; `tools/typecheck-witness.sh` after every commit; a pushed shard
run where a step changes what the e2e set reads, before the next spirit starts; a scratch root and a
scratch `HOME` for anything that writes custody; no local e2e. A step marked ''live'' changes a shape the
wire or a signature carries.

''The solo chain.'' Each of these holds the compose hunk in `open-node-vessel.ts` and
`open-browser-vessel.ts` while it runs, and no other node lane lands beside it: S, then K's seat, flip,
rename, scopes and founding act, then N's sealing and self-contracts, then W's three live steps, then W's
dials, then E, then O1's working address through its switch, then H's hosting act through its strangers' dial, then X.

!!! S ~ the custody seal (SUBSTRATE; running)
Its state and its remaining steps read in #/the-road's SUBSTRATE block, and nowhere else. It ends on the retirement of the passphrase lifecycle and on the fold's live proof.

!!! G ~ ground (waits on nothing; rides beside every train on disjoint files)
The rows of #/the-loops' GROUND group, tests-only work first. Riskiest: the summons cures, which touch what a verb's effect means.

!!! K ~ R-CHARTER, stage one: the seat (waits on S whole)
# ''Landed ahead'': the mesh charter fixture (`packages/lararium-mesh/tests/charter-fixture.ts`) and the cold-key card codec (`cold-key-card.ts`), which stays out of the barrel until the flip.
# The node, CLI and tool fixtures funnel through the same factory.
# The sealed seat-key store, on the custody holder.
# ''The seats sign with their own keys'', under the standing charter shape; each chair's next key rests sealed on disk until the flip.
# The rite's seam: two inner functions hold every next-key line.
# ''THE FLIP'', one assembled commit: per-seat cold digests and threshold, the seat-roll domain, the named refusal for an earlier shape, a card per chair with its read-back, and the reserve's retirement.
# The cold-key rehearsal.
# One name for a Nexus: one AID constructor, `nexus-<sha>`, the chair label, the cadence inception.
# The seed carries no version: the ONE genesis re-bake of this train, with the untracked CAS in the same commit.
# The floor key commits no next key.
# Edges and scopes commit to the Nexus AID; the sentinel re-keys.
# Per-Nexus keys mint at random, with the signed hand-over.
# A PersonaGroup founds as a Keyhive Group, so a revocation rolls the keys of every bag the group reaches.
# ''The Stable founding act'' for a hearth; the herm and joiner rites stay.
# Canon and the runbook.
''Riskiest'': the flip, which crosses three packages; then the founding act, since every e2e founds through it. The read-back stand-in must check more than the scratch marker: a copied marker on a root sealed under another passphrase refuses.

!!! N ~ R-CHARTER, stage two: the Nexus founding act (waits on K whole)
# `seal cofound open`: a seat key, a cold card, and an offer of public material that names the charter law and the release manifest's addresses.
# `seal cofound join`: the founder types the other seat's fingerprint as heard; it composes the genesis and half-signs.
# `seal cofound seal`, with every seated key's inception signature.
# The partial and cosign door: a partial carries the whole act image; a stale partial and a replay refuse.
# The founders' self-contracts and the two-seat roll.
# The roll that adds a seat, with the new holder's contract; a passed chair after it.
# The two-root witness, one process and two custody trees, carrying files alone.
# Canon.
''Riskiest'': the sealing step, which makes inception signatures a law every fixture meets.

!!! P ~ the Kahu plane around the train (its first three take no identity bytes and may run beside S and K)
# The steward signer.
# The carriage verifier holds the root.
# Realms and selected-realm routing.
# ''After N'': the chartered classes and exact-bytes promotion; Kahu-cabal admission and the cabal access path; R-KAHU.
# The cadence offers, which may follow the ceremony.
''Riskiest'': the steward signer, proven by the docker `meme` scenario by hand as well as by a shard.

!!! W ~ the wire and the face proof, one socket cutover (waits on K; its pure steps may start early)
# ''Landed ahead'', each a pure module out of the barrel, specified in code and reached by no production caller: Noise IK (`noise-ik.ts`); the proof subjects (`face-proof-subjects.ts`); private authority with the withdrawal fold and the chain check (`face-authority.ts`); the session signer (`session-signer.ts`); the session face supplier (`session-face.ts`); the gate bundle (`gate-bundle.ts`); the exchange's subjects (`gate-exchange.ts`); the gate behind interfaces, around the chain check and its six verdicts (`face-gate.ts`); the dialer (`face-dial.ts`).
# ''Landed ahead'': the handshake funnel. Every test that speaks the handshake goes through one helper (`gate-dial-fixture.ts`, in mesh and in node), and `gate-dial-funnel.test.ts` holds the line; the cutover edits that helper and the old wire's own vectors.
# ''Live'': the admit signs what it carries (after N's cosign door, which shares `nexus-contract.ts`).
# ''Live'': the fleet-join door; add-a-face; the bare seal import goes.
# ''Live, THE SOCKET CUTOVER'', one assembled commit: both dialers, the gate, the sorter, the ring's lookup by face subject; `lar:challenge`, the ContactCard proof and every vessel-key gate proof leave; the floor announcement signs under the wire key; the gate verifies a hand-over.
# One dial per (hearth, Nexus).
# The sibling channel at face scope.
# Canon.
''Riskiest'': the cutover; an old-wire dialer must draw no byte, and node and browser must both cross after it.

!!! E ~ the ember (waits on W's join door; lands before the fence)
# A design round first, on paper: a SERVING key, wrapped by the vessel key, wraps the rows a gate needs, and the ember's slot wraps that key alone, so an ember-raised vessel opens no seat key, persona root or cold row.
# The serving tier.
# The ember pin.
# The raise count, the record and the removal.
# Canon.
''Riskiest'': the design may turn out to need a signed shape, since the removal act rides the face's log.

!!! O1 ~ ONE FACE's sessions (its contract landed; the working address onward waits on W's cutover)
# ''Landed ahead'': the session contract in mesh (`session-contract.ts`); the scoped document view (`session-document-view.ts`), the one recipe resolver's surface resolution (`surface-recipe.ts`, `resolveSurfaceRecipe`) and the pool's surface door (`mountSurface`), each specified in code and reached by no production caller.
# The scoped document view's compose hunks: the share verdict's caller, the leaf's one-way gate and the hearth's twin.
# The recipe resolver's compose hunks: both platforms resolve at surface mount.
# The working document's address.
# Node callers move to sessions.
# The durability receipt.
# The browser holder as owner.
# Browser surfaces and the control leg.
# The switch; the selector retires.
# The fleet view and removal.
''Riskiest'': the working address, where an attach that cannot stand refuses the boot.

!!! H ~ the hosted road's re-cut (its pure introduction landed; the rest waits on K's founding act and W's cutover, and lands whole before X)
# ''Landed ahead'': the introduction, pure (`introduction.ts`).
# The hosting act names the operator's seat and three dials; its bytes change once, before the fence.
# A walker's token buys a knock, and earns standing by the operator's answer alone.
# The door and the answer.
# The strangers' dial.
# Canon: one pass on the invite doctrine.
''Riskiest'': the hosting act's signer, an authority change.

!!! A ~ HARBOR's tail (waits on nothing but the operator's hands for its live steps)
# ''Landed ahead'': the issuer slot and its witness against a test authority.
# The reach face's code half.
# Per-name resolver records.
# Renewal.
# LAN discovery's network mode.
# One run of the mesh scenarios and the harbor walk on the current image.
# The release, last.
''Riskiest'': ports 53 and 443 and multicast on the first operator's machine stand unmeasured.

!!! V ~ recovery's owed verbs (after S; beside N)
# Guardian enrolment.
# The memory-card reader.
# The backup bundle, where S did not take it.
# The restore rehearsal, run before the ceremony.

!!! B ~ the browser rungs and the leaves
# Browser custody, after the seal's Keyhive step.
# The owed device measures, by hand.
# The phone's admission walk, after household HTTPS and the join door.
# Rung 4, after X's witness.

!!! X ~ TWO HEARTHS (waits on everything above)
# The automated witness: two vessels from one image digest, no volume in common, a courier that carries files alone; it proves two seeds, one AID on both sides, each founder held at the other's gate, an edit crossing both ways and reading back after each restart and unlock, a third root ADDED as a seat and contracted as a carrier, and a dormant node that wakes, imports the lineage and presents its admit.
# The browser leg.
# The runbook walk.
# ''The ceremony'', each line one act: a dress rehearsal alone with synthetic names; the old homes moved aside; the image pulled by digest and the manifest's addresses read aloud; each founds, writes the seed's card and reads it back; each unlocks; each opens a co-founding offer and hands it across; each joins on the fingerprint heard aloud and reads the AID aloud; each seals; each contracts by partial and cosign; each makes its faces and joins the shared realm; each wears a face in a tab, edits, and reads the other's edit; each restarts, unlocks and reads both again; the phones mint and scan; the cards go to two places.
''Riskiest'': paper. One mis-copied card freezes a two-seat Nexus at its first roll; the read-back and the rehearsal answer it.

!!! By hand, the operator's, each with the moment it falls due
* Read CI at every shard point; the controlling session pushes the green head.
* The registrar key limited to the one domain, API access switched on for it, the two files placed: before the first live issuance.
* The router hands out the resolver's address; ports 53 and 443 free on the node's LAN interface: before the phone's walk.
* The tablet and a phone in hand for the capability probe: before browser custody hardens.
* One real-LAN discovery run; the second machine with docker and the image pulled by digest: before the dress rehearsal.
* Paper and a pen for four cold-key cards, and two places to keep them: at the rehearsal, then the ceremony.
* Push and sign the release index: after the last re-bake and the last wire change.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/side-lanes>>

!! Side lanes ~ queued beside the road, each on its own files

* ''The shadow at the gates.'' The law of removal's reach stands whole at <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/kapae#/reach">> (operator ruling): four marked edges, two hands, rolls that carry shadows, a ledger that keeps what a reader counted, a consult at every gate, and keys that never outrun standing. <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/kapae#/what-the-code-holds">> names each part the code holds and each part that stays owed, and this carrier keeps no copy of that list. The cosign door's verdicts and envelope stand ready for train N's door to adopt. The sealed store's key roll subscribes to the seat's roll and lands with its own train.
* ''Handle resolver wiring and cross-log order.'' A Handle reader that holds no owner-head resolver trusts the inception alone. Owed: the resolver's wiring, where it must answer "the current, unsuperseded, un-vetoed head" and never "a key that once stood as head", and the order between a Handle's log and its owner's log.
* ''The clock cures.'' `lares watch --delete-grace` lets a wall clock decide a tombstone (`packages/lares-cli/src/commands/watch.ts`); the audit of each remaining contract, Cabal and Handle door runs relation by relation, never as a blind sweep (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/causal-island#/selected-contracts">>).
* ''The code lane.'' False source comments (`G6` of #/the-loops); a bug in the module trust gate (`packages/lararium-tw5/src/tw5-module-gate.ts`) and its missing positive-path vector; callers that still mount a layer default-writable (`operator-daemon-behavior.ts`, `daemon-vm-core.ts`); mesh tests that sit outside the type-check.
* ''The Harbor tail'': train A.
* ''Early starts beside the chain'': the Kahu plane's first three steps take no identity bytes (the steward signer, the carriage verifier's held root, realms with selected-realm routing); the handshake funnel and the proof subjects of train W; the node, CLI and tool fixtures funnel of train K.
* ''The small sweep.'' The memetic-wikitext plugin still ships `$:/config/ResilientRender`, a flag nothing reads; retiring it rebuilds the plugin and takes a labelled genesis re-bake. Two e2e files read the first `gate key:` line of a log (`tests/e2e/meme-realm-bag.test.ts`, `tests/e2e/arrival-surfaces.e2e.test.ts`), and the `awaitRendezvous` docblock in `tests/harness/instance.ts` describes an earlier boot order. Three source comments name a carrier that left (`packages/lararium-keyhive/src/face-grant-record.ts`, `packages/lararium-keyhive/tests/archive-floor-write.test.ts`, `tests/e2e/meme-realm-bag.test.ts`); its law rests at <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/api/personal-slot">>. Five `Meme:` headers and two package notes name the shift ledger, which left (`packages/lares-cli/src/commands/watch.ts`, `commands/ingest.ts`, `packages/lares-cli/src/ingest-core.ts`, `packages/lararium-tw5/src/delete-gate.ts`, `packages/lararium-node/tests/ingest-verb.test.ts`, `packages/SPRINT-01-GENESIS-MESH.md`, `packages/.shelf/HANDOFF.md`); its procedures rest at <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/working-procedures">>.
* ''Band-ladder residue'': one five-band ladder, the measure-servo aliases in `ffz-project.ts`, the `lar_feedback` output field name. It rides the Sensorium's wait, and a frame inside it may heal at any time.
* ''The capture lane's era ruling'': #/open.
* ''Sealed-store step 2'': the durable lockbox store and chunk index, the Keyhive wrap of a content key, and the content-key holder that `cad-seal` and the key roll ask (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/sealed-store">>).

!!! Off this road, held by name
* ''Grammar'': tangle, the putback law and the tongue fold wait on a real return trip and a whole regeneration of `packages/tree-sitter-memetic-wikitext` against the released grammar; that regeneration also unlocks publication. A relay-stream profile (the SYN-framed batch), a carrier seal with a computed check, and EOT targeting stay held in reserve. The grammar watch reads in <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/grammar-watch">>.
* ''Publication'': the `text/markdown; variant=memetic-markdown` registration, the provisional `lar` scheme after `lar-uri` gains its Security section, the vendor media type, and the drafts. The standalone plugin artifact ships from `packages/lararium-tw5/plugins/standalone/`.
* ''The live wiki's floors'': exercise the quoteblock floor at both grains, the child gate and the persisted parallel drafts against real concurrent browser saves, and turn every surprise into a test.
* ''A standing whole-tree gate'' runs as a spirit pass, never as a CLI verb or a trigger.
* ''The ahi-kā knobs'' (the hysteresis gap, the commons-against-hearth exemption) wait on an estimator fit; no ruling stands owed.
* ''Future vessels'' (native mobile, Mudlet, Unreal) enter one at a time, each declaring whether it hosts a sovereign vessel or attaches a surface to a named one.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/fresh-start>>

!! The fresh start ~ by hand, reversible, never a command

NO pave or wipe command stands (operator-ruled): such a command carries too much risk. In early alpha a fresh
START still reads pono when it runs BY HAND: MOVE the old homes aside — rename them, never delete them, so
the move stays reversible — then found fresh on the re-found build. Valuable data lives in git, in the
private `claude-backup` repository, or on `D:`; a vessel home holds nothing that only it holds.

A fresh machine needs no move: a fresh vessel seeds from the tracked `bags/` and the committed `genesis/`
(`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/founding-runbook#/fresh-state`).

The homes to move: the ones the OLD build's resolvers name — the `~/.lares` home, the XDG data homes for
`lares` and `lararium`, and the state home — asked of the old build at the moment of moving, never
enumerated by hand. A founding refuses a store that holds an earlier shape (`OldShapeRefusal`, before any
route gets asked and before any write), which keeps an accidental founding off any home left unmoved. Other
Nexuses rejoin through presented admits; every old admit names an old AID and reads dead by construction.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/open>>

!! Open ~ what the operator still owns

!!! Seats, custody and recovery
# ''Guardians and recovery.'' Guardian count and threshold at enrolment, request authentication, the veto, a person's death and succession, the catastrophe rite and any third key, and a Handle's DNS binding stand open at <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/kahu#/seed-and-nexus">>.
# ''The backup bundle.'' What a per-face sealed bundle holds, which verb restores it, and whether the seal train or recovery's verbs build it. Lean: one bundle per face, so faces stay unlinked on the backup medium, built in the seal train.
# ''A sealed receipt manifest for carriage.'' It would let a root restored from paper re-open its carriage after device loss — and would turn carriage toward the backup W rules it never becomes. The lenses split; re-opening W needs the operator's turned key.
# ''Carriage across leaves.'' A guest-held carry-claim proven at the carry door would let carriage follow a guest across leaves — a second relation and a second domain. Lean: not built.
# ''The fork-resolve act's shape.'' The seal record holds one predecessor. A ruling after the fence costs a migration, and the dormant node's shattered-Nexus case waits on it.
# ''The re-seal proof.'' Name the causal record that maps old ciphertext to its replacement.
# ''A recovered face's earlier content'' in the sealed store, parked until the store's first three questions settle; and the reading of "delegated keys" for cloud carriers, deferred with them.
# ''House leans the operator may overturn'': the floor vessel key drops its next-key commitment; the long-silent device rule; the strangers' dial drops the newest arrival (#/decisions); the seal's standing leans (`S7` of #/the-loops).

!!! Planes and offerings
# ''The Offering Antigen scope'', and the charter-inception identity under it: identical rosters share a genesis seal epoch CID, and the Nexus AID the charter train mints bears on that premise (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/research/offering-antigen-scope-decision-record">>). No scope field and no enforcement land before the ruling. Beside it: the offering's `offer` and `witness` caps against the Lamplighter stack.
# ''The crossing record.'' Its durable emission threshold (lean: authority, vessel, federation and externally meaningful-effect boundaries alone), and whether a destination receipt always signs separately (lean: yes).
# ''Engine cadence'': who holds a cadence share; whether one daemon hosts islands at two engine epochs; whether partial conformance lands before `kahuli engine` un-holds (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/kahu#/contract">>).
# ''Grammar submissions'': whether the Nexus Kahu or the corpus-kahu receive them.
# ''DNS custody past the credential'': delegated `_acme-challenge`, record custody, the ACME account and CAA travel as one question (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/bounded-reach-contract">>). With it: whether a host timer or a hand runs renewal, and the answer for a phone that forces encrypted DNS.
# ''The crossroads mirror's filter'' (`G21` of #/the-loops).
# ''Removal's reach.'' The model stands ruled (#/rulings; <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/kapae#/four-edges">>). Seven questions stay the operator's, each with the house's lean. Whether an edge act may ever use the emergency class (lean: never). Whether a realm's quorum reads off the charter it stands under or off a charter of the realm's own (lean: the charter it stands under, until a realm seats its own). Whether a seated member under a member shadow keeps a seat's signature until the next roll (lean: yes, a seat leaves by a roll alone). What a recovery council holds after a mutual removal (lean: nothing built; the fork stands as the one exit). Whether a holder's key reads at its log's current head, so a recovered face keeps its edges (lean: yes, owed with the resolver of #/side-lanes). Whether a realm's boards key on the realm's own id, as built, or on the Nexus that carries it (lean: the realm, so a removal's record stays among its parties). Whether a counted raise moves the keys while a lift still races it (lean: yes, remove-wins reaches the keys, and a lift then seats afresh). Two more came with the key side. What removes a seat no standing hand can revoke, the founding vessel's own among them (lean: a fresh group, at the re-founding that moves the PersonaGroup to a Keyhive group). Whether a vessel that holds no revoke authority goes on trying a raise until it sees the seat leave (lean: yes, and each try hands the roll on again, so the content key rolls whoever revokes the seat).
# ''The self-slot inner ring.'' Wiring it freezes a naming: a bag URL through a live ring hashes to seed its document, and a re-name costs a re-founding. Lean: widen the bridge first, and wire the ring on an explicit ruling alone.

!!! Shore, grammar and code
# ''The ungated slot child.'' A slot child's native save never grades; three child-edit shapes stand marked as the operator's call (`packages/lararium-tw5/tests/meme-backstop.test.ts`; <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/syncer-back-parity">>).
# ''Ruling-gated mesh modules'' (listed in the header of `packages/lararium-mesh/src/index.ts`): `recipe`, `readiness`, `reaction-graph`, `pronaos`, `offering-inspection`. Each moves or stays by ruling alone.
# ''The capture cell'' sits apart for review in `packages/lararium-mesh/src/capture/`, `packages/lararium-node/src/capture/`, `packages/lararium-tw5/src/capture/` and `packages/lares-cli/src/commands/capture/`. Canon places capture in Python per stream with the TS daemon coordinating alone (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/api/capture-annotation-model">>), while the TS cell carries the live path. Rule: retire it to Python, or re-home it.
# ''Receipt names and verb capabilities.'' Whether a receipt's address follows the house's own kind nouns or the content-addressed surface; and the table that maps each routed verb to its capability, where `deriveRoutedCap` answers for every routed verb today (`packages/lararium-tw5/src/verb-local-dispatch.ts`).
# ''Rulings that rest in their own carriers'': the promotion receipt's fields (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/canon-boundary">>), the one-of-one mantle (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/handle-card">>), the lease's questions (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/realm-bag-brief">>), and the offering's questions (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/heraldry">>).
# ''Two Kairoses.'' The fiction names KAIROS as a watcher that speaks unasked; the code's Kairos pet-names an unbuilt entity that refreshes an OAuth grant at the right moment (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/reach-plane">>). One entity, or two that share a name?
# ''The disk watcher's reach.'' Whether the watcher may tombstone a carrier whose file vanished, by itself; today a wall-clock grace decides (#/side-lanes, the clock cures).
# ''Alerts and shadows.'' Whether a disk conflict that arrives while no wiki stands pinned raises its alert at the next pin; whether a hand that deletes its override of a shadow leaves a delete, where today the shadow's text gets saved as a record; whether the page warns when a browser has joined no face.
# ''The confirm door upstream.'' The fork asks its questions through the wiki itself (`$tw.utils.confirm`, `tm-confirm`). Owed before a donation: the order of actions after a confirm, a switch for a blocking prompt, and one squashed change. The withdrawn render boundary's upstream pull request, if it still stands open, advertises a design the fork backed out.
# ''One sentence for the `CLAUDE.md` adapter note'', the operator's to place: the CLI's ingest, watch and REPACK derive against `LAR_BAGS` and `LAR_WIKIS`, so "read neither" holds for the daemon's projection mirrors alone.

